# Repository-root ignores.
#
# `frontend/` and `backend/` carry their own .gitignore files; this one covers the things
# that sit outside both — the documentation tooling, and downloaded artefacts that land in
# the working directory and are easy to sweep into a commit with `git add -A`.

# Diagram rendering toolchain. Installed on demand by `npm install` inside docs/diagrams and
# regenerated from docs/diagrams/package.json — ~425 MB of Chromium and WebAssembly that must
# never enter the history. The rendered .svg and .png files ARE committed: they are the
# deliverable, and a reader must not need a toolchain to see a diagram.
docs/diagrams/node_modules/
docs/diagrams/.tmp/
docs/diagrams/package-lock.json

# Downloaded installers and packages. A stray 52 MB .deb committed once stays in the history
# for good, even after a later delete.
*.deb
*.rpm
*.dmg
*.msi

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Report source material. NOT pushable:
#  - "Assessment Brief.pdf" states on its own first page that it must not be passed to third
#    parties or posted on any website. A hosted repository is a website.
#  - "sample report.pdf" is another team's submitted coursework.
#  - The .docx draft is a binary that rewrites wholesale on every edit.
# Git history is permanent in practice, so these are ignored before the first commit rather
# than deleted in a later one.
docs/report/*.pdf
docs/report/*.docx
